# Hypnos backend — example requests (from README.md)
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and the JetBrains HTTP Client.
# Each request is separated by "###"; click "Send Request" above a block to run it.

@host = http://localhost:8888
# Only checked when the server has api_keys / HYPNOS_API_KEYS set.
@apiKey = 

### 1. Inspect 3-Tier Memory Status
GET {{host}}/v1/memory/status
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}


### 2. Text Generation (gemma4:26b-q4)
POST {{host}}/v1/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "gemma4:26b-q4",
  "messages": [
    { "role": "user", "content": "Explain Gemma 4 hybrid sliding window attention." }
  ],
  "max_tokens": 256
}


### 2b. Vision Generation (gemma4:26b-q4 also accepts image_url content parts)
POST {{host}}/v1/chat/completions
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "gemma4:26b-q4",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
        { "type": "text", "text": "What is in this image?" },
        { "type": "image_url", "image_url": { "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3a/Cat03.jpg" } }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_tokens": 256
}


### 3. Audio Transcription / STT (gemma4:e4b-q4)
# Place a sample.wav next to this file (or change the path below).
POST {{host}}/v1/audio/transcriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HypnosBoundary

------HypnosBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="model"

gemma4:e4b-q4
------HypnosBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.wav"
Content-Type: audio/wav

< ./sample.wav
------HypnosBoundary--


### 4. Text-to-Speech (kokoro-82m-q4 — pinned in Tier 1 VRAM)
# Response body is audio; REST Client lets you save it via "Save Response Body".
POST {{host}}/v1/audio/speech
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "kokoro-82m-q4",
  "input": "Hello from Hypnos!",
  "voice": "alloy"
}


### 5. Embeddings (gemmaembedding2 — pinned in Tier 1 VRAM)
POST {{host}}/v1/embeddings
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "gemmaembedding2",
  "input": ["3-tier GPU memory management"]
}


### 6. Image Generation (moss-image)
POST {{host}}/v1/images/generations
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "moss-image",
  "prompt": "A futuristic Rust crab managing GPU memory tiers"
}


### 7. Document Conversion (docling, Hypnos extension)
# Place a sample.pdf next to this file. Optional parts: pages ("2-5"), ocr (true/false),
# output_format (markdown/json), stream (true: one event per page), describe_pictures (a vision model).
POST {{host}}/v1/documents/convert
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HypnosBoundary

------HypnosBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="model"

docling
------HypnosBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="describe_pictures"

gemma4:e4b-q4
------HypnosBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="return_pictures"

true
------HypnosBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample.pdf
------HypnosBoundary--

### 7b. Pictures of a `return_pictures` conversion (use the `id` from the response above)
# The list carries the metadata; a single picture adds its base64 `image`. `?format=image`
# returns the bare image. DELETE releases them before `server.document_pictures_ttl_secs`.
GET {{host}}/v1/documents/doc-REPLACE-ME/pictures
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{host}}/v1/documents/doc-REPLACE-ME/pictures/1
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

###
GET {{host}}/v1/documents/doc-REPLACE-ME/pictures/1?format=image
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

###
DELETE {{host}}/v1/documents/doc-REPLACE-ME
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}


### 7c. Take a model out of service / put it back (not persisted to the config)
POST {{host}}/v1/models/gemma4:e4b-q4/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

###
POST {{host}}/v1/models/gemma4:e4b-q4/enable
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

### 8. Entity Extraction (gliner2.5-multi, Hypnos extension)
# Zero-shot: any labels. `input` takes one text or a list; threshold defaults to 0.5.
POST {{host}}/v1/entities
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "gliner2.5-multi",
  "input": ["Mario Rossi works in Milan for Ferrari.", "Tim Cook announced the iPhone 17 in Cupertino."],
  "labels": ["person", "city", "company", "product"],
  "threshold": 0.5
}
